  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Close the Gap: Sufficient, Competent and Motivated Nurses and Midwives - Rwanda</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Norwegian Nurses Organisation (NNO/NSF) aims to create democratic, accountable, inclusive and sustainable organisations for nurses and midwives in four countries in Africa. Cooperation with Rwanda Nurses and Midwives Union (RNMU) goes back to 2013. The aim for this project period is to build the financial and organisational  sustainability of RNMU, and their capacity as an effective watchdog and advocate for nurses and midwives and solution provider for the government, contributing to a stronger and more resilient health system to deliver Universal Health Coverage (UHC) and good health for all in Rwanda. The project includes a focus on nurses and midwives&#x2019; equal opportunity to leadership training and positions (gender equality) and the rights of nurses and midwives with disabilities. It also aims to train nurses and midwives in health-related climate adaptation, in the face of increased climate change and extreme weather related health emergencies. Finally, the project aims to train the nurses and midwives to provide the best possible assistance to patients with disabilities and with SRHR to female patients.</narrative>
  </description>
